From 4e425b49514750b5228f91bc06feb0d0c35855e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:11:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] scheduler v2: faster unit evaluation, per-pool profile
 stores, docs

* eval_sums/next_unit: per-P cached contiguous profile rows and inlined
  time law and cells (next_unit 0.33 -> 0.18 ms; a 1 CPU-year forecast
  over the 378k-P pool simulates in ~3.5 min); node predictions only for
  launched units.
* Profiles live in profiles_6/<pool kind>-<key>/, so changing the pool
  options never discards a filled store.
* A gap of sums below the model's first valid point (e.g. between ceil(S0)
  and the S_min another search started from) counts as covered.
* forecast --shipped (prior calibration and time law, no per-P factors);
  regression mode reads .jsonl.gz unit files too.
* Docstring and README describe the analytic model, the pool and the new
  commands.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GSaYLGdzq6d82nBLeSZFgB
